   226	
   227	### Additive policy
   228	
   229	`gnd evolve preview --policy additive` judges every operation by one matrix over (locator kind,
   230	operation kind). The policy keeps every fact already admitted under the current model that GND
   231	can see (sample rows, a declared reference population, a `population` artifact, `--populated`;
   232	under `--check-population`, relative to that file) interpretable under the candidate: nothing existing is renamed, deleted or changed, and no
   233	constraint on a populated fact type is added or strengthened. This table and the strengthening list
   234	are the policy's one normative home; `gnd.evolve.policy` implements them, and preview and apply
   235	share that implementation.
   236	
   237	**Populated.** A fact type is populated when it has `sample_population` rows, when a declared
   238	reference population owns it, when a `population` artifact locator in the proposal references
   239	`fact_types[ID]`, or when `--populated ID` names it. A `--populated` id that names no fact type of
   240	the current model exits `3`. A constraint's subjects are its host fact type, when it is hosted on
   241	one, and the fact types its role references and rule atoms name, in `before` and `after` alike, and, for a constraint that ranges
   242	over an object type without a role (`value` or `cardinality` with `object_type` and no `role_ref`,
   243	`subtype-partition`'s `supertype` and `subtypes`), every fact type with a role played by that
   244	object type, by a subtype of it, or by an entity it identifies as reference value type. It counts
   245	as populated when **any** subject is. A fact type the same proposal adds is never populated. A `modify` of an element the
   246	same proposal adds is judged like any other `modify`: declare the element once, in its final shape.
   247	
   248	| Locator | add | modify | rename | delete |
   249	|---|---|---|---|---|
   250	| `object_types` element | admitted | admitted iff the diff is confined to `description` and `provenance.rationale`; otherwise `object_types.modify` | `object_types.rename` | `object_types.delete` |
   251	| `fact_types` element | admitted | admitted iff the diff is confined to `provenance.rationale`; otherwise `fact_types.modify` (a changed reading, role list, constraint or sample row included) | `fact_types.rename` | `fact_types.delete` |
   252	| `operations` element | the operations gate's (exit `18`) | pre-empted by the gate | pre-empted | pre-empted |
   253	| role | admitted on a fact type the same proposal adds; otherwise `role.add` | `role.modify` | `role.rename` | `role.delete` |
   254	| constraint, subject not populated | admitted | admitted | pre-empted: a constraint has no stable id to rename (exit `3` at proposal read) | admitted |
   255	| constraint, subject populated | `constraint.populated.add` | admitted iff every differing key weakens or is `rationale` (or `provenance.reviewed_in`); otherwise `constraint.populated.modify` | pre-empted | admitted |
   256	| model identity | — | `model_identity.modify` | — | — |
   257	| source document | admitted | `source_document.modify` | pre-empted: refused at proposal read (`3`) | `source_document.delete` |
   258	
   259	An include `repin-include` is refused by the additive policy with `include.repin-include`; other include mutations are refused at proposal read.
   260	
   261	An element `modify` replaces the whole element, so its cell is an allow-list over the dotted paths
   262	at which `before` and `after` differ; a path beneath an admitted key (`description.summary`) is
   263	admitted.
   264	
   265	**Strengthening and weakening**, per differing key of a constraint `modify`. Any other differing
   266	key (`type`, `role`, `role_ref`, `object_type`, a role sequence, `source`, `owner`, `status` to
   267	`rejected`, `allowed` against `range`, a `ranges` list of changed length, an unknown key) is
   268	neither, and refused on a populated subject.
   269	
   270	| Key | Strengthening | Weakening |
   271	|---|---|---|
   272	| `roles` (uniqueness only; a frequency projection change is neither) | proper subset | proper superset |
   273	| `allowed` (value) | proper subset | proper superset |
   274	| `range.min`, `ranges[i].min`, `bound.min` | raised, or added | lowered, or removed |
   275	| `range.max`, `ranges[i].max`, `bound.max` | lowered, or added | raised, or removed |
   276	| `min_inclusive`, `max_inclusive` | `true` to `false` | `false` to `true` |
   277	| `modality` | `deontic` to `alethic` | `alethic` to `deontic` |
   278	| `status` | `proposed` to `confirmed` | `confirmed` to `proposed` |
   279	
   280	D-12 runs first, so a changed constraint still has to be llm-inferred, sample or common-sense
   281	and proposed/deontic, user-supplied/confirmed, or a reviewed induced confirmation; the policy
   282	judges what D-12 admits.
   283	
   284	A locator kind the matrix has no row for is refused, never admitted: the policy raises
   285	`EvolutionPolicyGapError`, which exits `3` by type.
   286	
   287	**Order.** Pending state (`11`), stale identity (`11`), the operations gate (`18`), candidate
   288	validation, replay equality and D-12 (`3`), then the policy. A preview with issues is still written
   289	to `--out`, for review, and the command exits `3`.
   290	
   291	**Apply.** The additive guarantee holds when `apply` repeats the preview's `--policy` and
   292	`--populated`. The command compares its options with the reviewed preview's `policy` and
   293	`populated_args` before the retry branch and the fresh/reviewed equality and exits `3` when they differ, in either direction; it then
   294	rebuilds the preview with those options, so a preview whose `policy_issues` were edited and whose
   295	digest was recomputed differs from the fresh one and exits `11`. `EvolutionService.apply` re-runs
   296	the policy on the bytes it is about to publish and refuses with `3` on any issue, naming the
   297	operation index and cell; it never reads the preview's issue list. A preview stripped of every
   298	policy field and applied without `--policy` publishes as a policy-free preview.
   299	
   300	#### Population check
   301	
   302	`--check-population FILE` (with `--policy additive`; alone it exits `3`) lets the policy admit a
   303	constraint it would refuse as `constraint.populated.add`, or as a `constraint.populated.modify` whose
   304	differing keys all strengthen, weaken or are admitted, on the evidence of one population file. It
   305	clears that refusal only when all of these hold:
   306	
   307	1. the constraint after the operation is `status: proposed` and `modality: deontic`;
   308	2. every populated subject of the constraint (the subjects defined under **Populated**) has at least
   309	   one fact in the file, and no subject has `sample_population` rows in the current model, which the
   310	   checker does not see;
   311	3. that constraint's own verdict, from one `gnd.checker.check` of the candidate model over the file,
   312	   is `pass`. `warning` (how a deontic violation is reported), `fail`, `unchecked` and `vacuous` leave
   313	   the refusal. Other constraints' verdicts do not matter, and the `gnd check` exit band is never
   314	   consulted.
